0065 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186124541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050065 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186124576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050065 #edb/ref 1031 "The Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050065 #edb/ref 1033 1961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050065 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2a6bebd4-c41b-566e-8d69-b14df5637cea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1031 "Expressing the Coordinates of a Vector in a Given Basis" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1033 1864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050638 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5ae18ce0-90c2-55f7-8d81-bd5949f05aa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119631 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119631 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ if $\\,\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ and\n![](images/0e/0ef553621590325eecc2b429ffa09cd0cd4645a2653b3fd93db25f711676c132.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119631 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a0ea798-5125-5d0e-a755-96bf9af5f543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119631 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that any vector in  $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,\\mathcal{B}.$ Since we are told that ![](images/93/93ae6d0ad6dbd6036c99e5d2fcb55789fef9b2e576300f13b43ed561856fa218.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(-1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,3\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119632 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119632 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/d0/d094c88349d0a2c8707fafcf1a1cd63de028d56358ba8019b0527e77091e51d5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119632 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c7237cd-c655-575f-83ac-7a0891c336b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119632 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n![](images/14/14c42b3d306468a8a17f5ffaef535dd39c6d5fdb079366d9f495774b6e019815.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix above corresponds to the following system of equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2 =-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx_1 + 3 \\left( -1 \\right)  = -5\n\\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad\nx_1 = -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/5e/5e92e3cfdbf8d1c81be5b47124df9992d98835668154a50ece28cce8941860ca.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119633 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4825" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119633 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2, \\mathbf{b}_3 \\},$ where\n![](images/4e/4eb4b3533453f1a2c08c98bb8e6fd63e3f93563a4a2d56ecc0c0caef225b82e3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119633 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90f07e38-405a-5f79-8501-0b4dfb8fa4c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119633 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above system as an augmented matrix $M$ and reducing using Gaussian elimination, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -9{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=7 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{x}_{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 =2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-9x_2 - 2 = 7 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_2=-1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+3(-1) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_1 = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/61/61d8401f40152a8eaeb30d3dc55d9548cac508b6239a9a70e99fbed9e271805b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119674 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119674 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/dc/dc9eaa6ef7632676a920b5032f9af213dba581552c2337471b4657a0fc26ad2f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119674 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a79126f2-e26c-5929-93d8-825d85b9a438" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119674 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n![](images/9e/9ed5651afa52eedb2786ed4e46875636e9263f955f9c99db563ff3ebe629275f.png)\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n![](images/59/5972542de3b4c7c622177994f83239fb14f4ea3242cdc164a88b102b780b7da9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120379 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186247247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186391910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119820 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Vector 